title: MikroTik NTP Client
agents: mikrotik
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 NTP client of a MikroTik RouterOS 7 device ({/system/ntp/client}).

 Reported: synchronisation status ({WARN} if not {synchronized}), the
 server the device is synchronized with, the absolute time offset
 (default {WARN} at 200 ms, {CRIT} at 500 ms) and the stratum (default
 {WARN} at 10, {CRIT} at 15). Mode, servers, VRF and frequency drift are
 shown in the details. The API reports the offset as a plain number in
 milliseconds. A disabled NTP client is {WARN}. Levels and states via the
 rule {MikroTik NTP Client}.

 To connect to the MikroTik device a special datasource program is
 used: {MikroTik RouterOS} in Setup > Agents > Other integrations,
 module "NTP client". The module is opt-in, "all" does not include it.

perfdata:
 Time offset.

inventory:
 One service if the NTP client is enabled.
